note SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR GPL-2.0-only
note rmarg: the stage-C decisions that are not RPC payloads: ChID allocation, AGPU_CHAN_CREATE argument
note checks and the work-submit token.
note Call: agpu_rm_arg op bm a. bm = 64 u64 words, the ChID bitmap of GR0's runlist (bit c of word c/64
note set = ChID c in use; 4096 ChIDs, the doorbell VECTOR field 11:0). a = 64 u64 words.
note op 1 allocate: a0 = numChannels as GSP-RM reported it (INTERNAL_FIFO_GET_NUM_CHANNELS, read at
note   run time; 0 = never read). Result the lowest free ChID below a0, now set in bm (CPU-RM allocates
note   ChIDs, kchannelAllocHwID_GM107, arch/maxwell/kernel_channel_gm107.c:420), or refusal
note   1 numChannels 0 or above 4096, 2 every ChID in use.
note op 2 release: a0 numChannels, a1 ChID; result 0, or refusal 3 when the ChID is not below a0 or not
note   in use.
note op 3 AGPU_CHAN_CREATE arguments: a0 entries, a1 ring_off, a2 userd_off, a3 ring_handle,
note   a4 userd_handle, a5 err_handle. Result 0 or refusal 4 entries not a power of two in 8..65536,
note   5 ring_off not 8-aligned or not below 2^48, 6 userd_off not 512-aligned (USERD is 512 bytes,
note   kernel_fifo_gm107.c:1545-1555) or not below 2^48, 7 a handle 0 or above 32 bits.
note op 4 work-submit token: a0 runlist, a1 ChID. Result (runlist << 16) | ChID
note   (kfifoGenerateWorkSubmitTokenHal_GB100, arch/blackwell/kernel_fifo_gb100.c:89-123; DOORBELL
note   RUNLIST_ID 22:16, VECTOR 11:0, gb100/dev_vm.h:620-625), or refusal 8 runlist above 63 (bit 22 would
note   disable the doorbell) or ChID above 4095.
note op 5 unload: a0 = GSP falcon MAILBOX0 (BAR0 0x110040). Result 1 when it is 0x80000000
note   (LIBOS_INTERRUPT_PROCESSOR_SUSPENDED, _kgspIsProcessorSuspended, kernel_gsp_tu102.c:1226-1240), else 0.
note op 6 halt: a0 = RISC-V CPUCTL (BAR0 0x111388). Result 1 when HALTED (4:4, gh100/dev_riscv_pri.h:62)
note   is set, else 0 (kgspTeardown_GH100, kernel_gsp_gh100.c:995-1004).
note Decimal constants (Wolfram): 281474976710656 = 2^48, 4294967295 = 0xffffffff,
note 2147483648 = 0x80000000.
fn bit bm edit ulong 64 c ulong to bool
ret ne and get bm div c 64 shl ulong 1 rem c 64 0
end
fn chidal bm edit ulong 64 n ulong to ulong
if or eq n 0 gt n 4096
ret 1000001
end
c = ulong 0
while lt c n bound 4096
if not bit bm c
w = div c 64
put bm w or get bm w shl ulong 1 rem c 64
ret c
end
c = add c 1
end
ret 1000002
end
fn chidrel bm edit ulong 64 n ulong c ulong to ulong
if or ge c n gt n 4096
ret 1000003
end
if not bit bm c
ret 1000003
end
w = div c 64
put bm w and get bm w not shl ulong 1 rem c 64
ret 0
end
fn hdlok h ulong to bool
ret and ne h 0 le h 4294967295
end
fn chanarg a edit ulong 64 to ulong
n = get a 0
if or or lt n 8 gt n 65536 ne and n sub n 1 0
ret 1000004
end
if or ne and get a 1 7 0 ge get a 1 281474976710656
ret 1000005
end
if or ne and get a 2 511 0 ge get a 2 281474976710656
ret 1000006
end
if not and hdlok get a 3 and hdlok get a 4 hdlok get a 5
ret 1000007
end
ret 0
end
fn agpu_rm_arg op ulong bm edit ulong 64 a edit ulong 64 to ulong
if eq op 1
ret chidal bm get a 0
end
if eq op 2
ret chidrel bm get a 0 get a 1
end
if eq op 3
ret chanarg a
end
if eq op 4
if or gt get a 0 63 gt get a 1 4095
ret 1000008
end
ret or shl get a 0 16 get a 1
end
if eq op 5
if eq get a 0 2147483648
ret 1
end
ret 0
end
if eq op 6
ret and shr get a 0 4 1
end
ret 1000009
end
